instuection set for cpu11

(0000) BLK - Dosent do anything, Usefull for making timed things, although dependent on the clock speed, as it does not use any sort of delta time
(0001) HAL - Halts the program
(0010) LOD {d1} - Sets the accumilator to whatever $d1 is
(0011) CLR - clears and dumps the memory
(0100) 
(0101) LDA {d1} - Copy data from memory address $d1 into Accumulator
(0110) STA {d1} - Load Accumilator into memory address $d1
(0111) ADD {d1} - adds memory contents $d1 and accum together, for example d1= 00001001 accum= 10001010, answer= 10010011
